{"type":"response.output_text.done","timestamp":10275,"data":{"type":"response.output_text.done","content_index":0,"item_id":"msg_0287cf9c802e10590069c9a65c23d08190b3e3f19b4be0b2a3","logprobs":[],"output_index":1,"sequence_number":53,"text":"Paris is the capital of France, located in the north-central part of the country along the Seine River. It is widely known as a major global center of culture, art, fashion, gastronomy, commerce, and intellectual life. Historically, Paris grew from early settlement on the Île de la Cité and developed over centuries into one of Europe’s most influential cities. ([britannica.com](https://www.britannica.com/place/Paris))\n\nThe city is especially famous for its landmarks and neighborhoods, including the Eiffel Tower, Notre-Dame, the Louvre, Montmartre, the Latin Quarter, and the Champs-Élysées. Paris is also divided into 20 arrondissements, each with its own character and identity. ([en.wikipedia.org](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paris))\n\nIn short, Paris is often called the “City of Light” and stands out for its blend of history, architecture, museums, food, and everyday street life, making it one of the world’s most visited and recognizable cities. ([britannica.com](https://www.britannica.com/place/Paris))"}}
